# Expected DID Document for did:key:z6MkpTHR8VNsBxYAAWHut2Geadd9jSwuBV8xRoAnwWsdvktH.
# This is the key vendored by the project's did-test-suite submodule
# (third_party/testing/did/packages/did-core-test-server/suites/
# implementations/did-key-spruce.json — spruceid/ssi's did:key
# implementation, one of the "dids" it lists test fixtures for). That
# vendored JSON encodes the key as Ed25519VerificationKey2018 +
# publicKeyJwk (a DIFFERENT, older cryptosuite than the one this module
# targets), so it cannot be transcribed directly as our expected
# Ed25519VerificationKey2020 + publicKeyMultibase document. Instead this
# file assembles the expected document by hand-applying the SAME
# structural template the did-method-key spec demonstrates verbatim for
# the other two vectors in this directory (verificationMethod
# id/type/controller/publicKeyMultibase, plus authenticationMethod /
# assertionMethod / capabilityInvocationMethod / capabilityDelegationMethod
# each pointing at that verificationMethod's id) — substituting only this
# DID string. Not generated by DID.Key.fst. The raw public-key bytes were
# independently cross-checked (base58check decode of the multibase value
# matches the vendored fixture's publicKeyJwk.x, base64url-decoded) before
# this file was written, so the DID itself is confirmed genuine even
# though its 2018-suite JSON form is not directly reusable here.
# keyAgreement OMITTED (X25519 derivation deferred), same as the other
# two vectors.
